Our EDW primarily follows a Star Schema. The central fact table is fact_loans, and 
it is surrounded by dimensions such as dim_customers, dim_branches, dim_employees, 
and dim_loans. The source data first comes into the ODS layer. Customer data is loaded using SCD Type 1, 
where historical changes are not maintained. Branch data uses SCD Type 2, 
where we maintain historical versions using start_date, end_date, and is_current.

The loan data from ods_loans is combined with customer and branch dimensions
to populate fact_loans. During the fact load, we calculate measures and derived attributes 
such as loan duration, risk indicator, and high-value flag. Finally, fact_loan_summary
is populated from fact_loans by aggregating loan metrics based on branch and risk category.
Since the EDW contains multiple fact tables sharing dimensions, it can also be considered
a Fact Constellation or Galaxy Schema."

